    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0746" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363 Amiranian/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Merriam</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-04T09:00:00+03:25">January 4, 1937—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1. My 62, December 16, noon, and the Department’s 50, December 23, noon [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">6 p.m.</hi>]. Yesterday Hart and Clapp and the Iranian
                        <pb facs="0747" n="736" xml:id="pg736"/> Government signed two concession
                    agreements, one relating to oil exploration and development, the other to
                    construction and operation of pipe line. Will telegraph brief summary later.</p>
                <p>It proved unnecessary to act on paragraph 3 of No. 50. Crain<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d580-f1"/> was present in a purely notarial capacity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Merriam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="22" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>Earl T. Crain, Third Secretary of Legation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
